// Spelling-to-phoneme rules for Sardinian (sardu, sc)
// This file is UTF-8 encoded.
//
// The input is expected in the "Limba Sarda Comuna" (LSC) spelling
// (Regione Autonoma della Sardegna, 2006).  The pronunciation is the
// "sardo neutro" of the SINTESA project (Universita` di Cagliari,
// 2013-2015): it follows the LSC spelling and no local dialect.
// The rules were checked against the SINTESA lexicon (LGPL v3).
//
// Phonemes: see phsource/ph_sardinian.
//   E O   open mid vowels [ɛ ɔ];  e o  closed allophones [e o]
//   i#    <i> after c, g, sc before a vowel (spoken only if stressed)
//   E-    final e of the infinitives in -ere (dropped before a word)
//   n#    final n of -nt (the t is not spoken)
//   B D Q d. n. N M n^ tS dZ ts dz S Z r R
//   C:    long (geminate or semi-geminate) consonant
//
// Stress: on the penultimate vowel letter (as in LSC), unless the
// word has a written accent (à è ì ò ù).
//
// Metaphony ("adeguamentu vocàlicu", SINTESA ch. 2.2): <e o> are
// closed [e o] when the next deciding letter in the word is
// i, u, j, x or gn; the letter a (or the end of the word) keeps them
// open.  Consonants do not decide.  A closed e/o spreads the closing
// to an earlier e/o only when it is stressed or after the stress
// (fenòmenu [fe'nomenu], telèfonu [te'lef:onu]), not when it is
// before the stress (elementu [Ele'mentu], renessia [rEnes:'ia]).


